WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.801 --> 00:00:02.868
-I command you!

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.801
-Why should we listen to you?

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:06.167
[ Crowd shouting ]

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:08.334
-Because I...am...God!

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.167
[ All gasping, shouting ]

00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:18.033
♪♪

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.868
-So, you play God.
-Yes.

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:24.000
There was -- there was a thing
on that robe, on that cape,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.667
though, that was not safe
for television, I don't think.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:28.367
-Oh, really?
-But, great!

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:31.601
-Go back,
rewind and pause, kids.

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:33.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:35.434
I think we would've
got away with it, Bowen.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:36.767
-Damn!
-Oh.

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:39.167
-Sorry, Standards and Practices.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.000
-Well, guess what.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.067
It was hard finding a clip
from "Dicks: The Musical."

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:46.267
-I know, I'm sure.

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:47.601
-We didn't want
to have you on here

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:49.067
and show a 2 1/2-second clip.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:51.334
-Sure. You couldn't
have called it...

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.334
I can't -- I can't even come up
with an alternative

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:55.167
to "Dicks: The Musical"
that is safe for television.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:57.167
-This was a UCB show

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.400
that you were involved with
back in 2014?

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.968
-I was not involved.
I was just, like, a lowly,

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:03.968
lowly audience member.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:09.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.968
I was, but I saw it like
multiple times.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:14.767
And it was -- this was,
like, back in 2014, 2015.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.667
And it was Josh Sharp
and Aaron Jackson

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.834
who are in the movie
who play these twin brothers.

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:22.367
It's a gay "Parent Trap,"
basically, that's a musical.

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:24.934
And, but then they did
this show like once a month

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:27.334
and then it became
this, like, meeting ground

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:29.567
and this touchpoint for a lot
of queer comedians in the city,

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:31.267
like, who had never
really talked

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.701
to each other before that,

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:34.234
who didn't hang out,
and it was -- it was great.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:35.968
We all, like, went out to...
They said,

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:38.868
"We're doing a talk-back
at a bar around the corner."

00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:41.133
And it was just an excuse
for us to, like,

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:42.634
just talk and hang out.
-That's so nice.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:43.868
So, I'm assuming
when they reached out

00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:45.367
and said, "Bowen,
we'd like you to play God,"

00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:46.901
It was a quick yes.
-Quick yes.

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:48.267
And I'm really honored.

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:50.601
It's like, what, me,
Morgan Freeman,

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:52.534
Alanis Morissette,
and George Burns?

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:55.300
Like, that's a crazy...
-Yeah, those are the four gods.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.968
-Those are the -- That's
the Mount Rushmore of gods.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:01.567
We're like the "Sex and
the City" girls of Gods.

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:04.667
-How -- I mean, I know
you always do a lot of research

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.000
about a character
before you play it.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.634
What did you find
that drew you to God?

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:12.300
-Well, I read the entire Bible
cover to cover,

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.200
and in Aramaic.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.367
[ Laughter ]
No, I...I...

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:21.701
So, God in this movie is this,
like, really petulant

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:24.601
sort of gay entity.

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:26.934
And it got me thinking,
like, my way in was like,

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:30.100
God is kind of a messy queen,
you know?

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:34.601
Like, he's so dramatic,
floods the world,

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:37.167
makes it rain frogs.
That's campy.

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:38.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:41.000
Like, you know,
the whole Book of Job is him,

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.634
like, playing The Sims
on this one guy, like...

00:02:44.634 --> 00:02:46.400
You know?

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.467
So, I feel like that is --
this is a very, like,

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:51.734
it's a "new" portrayal of God,
but it's like, it's God

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:53.200
the way we understand God.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.067
-Yes, that we haven't
been able to admit

00:02:55.067 --> 00:02:56.567
that's what God
has been telling us.

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:58.267
-Exactly.
-And now you're finally like,

00:02:58.267 --> 00:02:59.701
let's just own it.
-And let's just own it.

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:02.834
Everyone's free to just call God
a messy queen from now on.

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:04.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.968
This is a great cast.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.267
Nathan Lane.
-Yes.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:08.501
-Megan Mullally is in it.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.133
-But really all anybody

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:11.801
who's seen the movie
is talking about is,

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:13.567
is the sewer boys.
-The sewer boys.

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:15.400
-So, the sewer boys
are these two characters

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.868
that belong to Nathan Lane
in the film.

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:19.601
-Yep. That's right.

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:22.200
-They're, like,
just prosthetic dudes.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.400
-Yes, they're real puppets.
They're prosthetic dudes.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.067
-Here's a good sense of
their actual size.

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:27.234
-That's right.

00:03:27.234 --> 00:03:30.067
So, that's them with us
on the red carpet.

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:31.400
I...

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:35.367
Someone made me hold one of them
on the red carpet,

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:37.234
and I wasn't --
I thought they were

00:03:37.234 --> 00:03:38.434
really adorable, really cute.

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:41.934
But then when I touched them,
they're...

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.400
Whoever made them,

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:48.701
made them out of, like, real
skin and bone, it seemed like.

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:50.367
I was like, this is vile.

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:51.634
But I'm curious --

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:53.100
You've lived in New York
a long time.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.434
Do you believe that
there is, like, a species,

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:58.200
a lateral species
of, like, sewer people?

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.200
Like, mole people?
What do you think?

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.434
-100%.
-Yes!

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:03.767
-Yeah. 100%.
-There has to be.

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:05.434
-And I think they're not
that upset about it.

00:04:05.434 --> 00:04:06.434
-No.
-Yeah.

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:07.634
-Great real estate down there.

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.767
-Yeah. I think they're great.
Like, absolutely.

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.434
They have so much space
and they're, like...

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:13.367
-It's by the train.
-It's by the train.

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:15.901
Talking about God,
you actually, as a kid,

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:18.033
wanted to make a deal
with the devil.

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:19.367
-Yes, I think...

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:23.868
I guess I admitted this
on a press thing for this movie.

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:25.234
Someone unlocked
a memory for me.

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:26.400
They said, "Did you ever sell...

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:27.734
Have you ever sold your soul
to the devil?"

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.567
I said, "Wait a minute,
I did!"

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:30.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:33.567
When I was like 11 years old,

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.567
there was an episode of
"The Simpsons" that was on.

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:37.234
It's called
"Bart Sells His Soul."

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:39.033
Season seven, episode four,

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:41.667
and written by Greg Daniels,

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:44.567
who we all know and love
from "The Office."

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:46.367
And Bart basically sells
his soul to Milhouse,

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:48.033
and then I think by the end
of the episode, he, like,

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:49.968
you know, asks Satan
to give it back.

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:51.667
And I was -- I watched that
in my basement,

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:54.501
being like, "You can do that?
Great!"

00:04:54.501 --> 00:04:56.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.501
-So, you did not watch the
episode as a cautionary tale.

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:03.400
-No, no. Purely encouraged.
And just had, like,

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.400
an imaginary conversation
with Satan.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.400
I think I just wanted
to play, like, a video game.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.667
I think I just wanted to play,
like, ironically,

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:12.167
like Diablo 2 or something.

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:14.667
And I got it, and I...

00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:17.501
And so he upheld his bargain,
and I think

00:05:17.501 --> 00:05:19.667
I'm still technically
locked into this deal.

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:21.167
-You seem fine, though.

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:24.767
-I don't know, I feel like
I come off soulless sometimes.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:27.434
Right, guys?
But I blame Greg Daniels

00:05:27.434 --> 00:05:29.567
for this Faustian
bargain, though.

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:31.801
-Yeah, well, you've got to
pin it on somebody.

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:33.300
You might as well pin it on him.
-He owes me a show.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.734
-Yeah, there you go.
Did you...Do you have any...

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:38.567
You know, I know, five months
of not doing "SNL."

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:40.200
Are there any sketches
you've come up with

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.868
over the years
that you have pitched

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:43.634
that you wish
had been received better?

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:46.767
-Oh, yeah. I mean,
just always, always, always.

00:05:46.767 --> 00:05:51.167
But the one that I think really,
really, like, got away from me

00:05:51.167 --> 00:05:54.701
was Jenna Ortega was here last
season, and at Monday pitch,

00:05:54.701 --> 00:05:59.234
I pitched her this thing where
she is a children's book author

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:04.200
and she writes a book
that's kind of like

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.534
"Can You Give a Mouse a Cookie."

00:06:05.534 --> 00:06:07.133
-"Can You Give a Mouse a Cookie"
is a great book.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.634
-Great book.
-And it's about how things just

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.167
get, like, sort of...
You give a mouse a cookie

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:11.567
and that's just the beginning
of the problem, yeah.

00:06:11.567 --> 00:06:12.901
-Just the beginning
of a problem.

00:06:12.901 --> 00:06:16.601
And I pitched her
a children's book title

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:18.934
that she could be
the author of, called

00:06:18.934 --> 00:06:20.767
"Can You Give a Bitch a Break?"

00:06:20.767 --> 00:06:22.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:25.934
And, didn't take.
Didn't take.

00:06:25.934 --> 00:06:27.734
-How could that not take?
-I know! I don't know.

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:29.334
-They've lost their minds
up there!

00:06:29.334 --> 00:06:31.000
-Exactly.
-Hey, thanks for being back.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.000
-Thanks for having me, Seth.
-I'm so happy "SNL" is back.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.167
I'm so happy you're back
in the building.

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:36.334
Bowen Yang!

00:06:36.334 --> 00:06:39.467
"SNL" premieres Saturday
on NBC and Peacock.

00:06:39.467 --> 00:06:41.200
"Dicks: The Musical"
is in select theaters now

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.367
and nationwide October 20th.

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:44.634
We'll be right back
with Jason Blum.

